  "enrollment": "One hosted runner per map and physical seat. Same runner and image for both packages, fresh containers per game. Both play the original to time or extinction, using their normal public entry throughout. Keep natural unseeded T=1 and the original 0.58s search.",
  "evidence_gate": "Four bound continuation tapes on two previous terrains. Each requires strictly positive gain in official margin and >=2 actual changed physical orders in the registered window. Net ground rent gain summed over maps must be positive. One student arm had 118/171 zero-depth returns. This qualifies a new-map test of the deployed policy without establishing a whole-game win.",
  "primary": "Wins, draws, losses, candidate and parent official final scores and signed margins by physical seat on both maps. Report all eight attempts, matched difference by map if both scores exist, ongoing and incomplete counts. Draws count as zero wins. No early outcome stop, depth filtering or sampling until win.",
  "timeouts": "Candidate call failure or timeout is a counted loss under ladder limits, opponent failure a counted forfeit win. With no official numeric score report null and separately state denominator of observed complete-game margins. Bilateral failure and infrastructure outcomes retain tickets, public timing and status; never impute a match score.",
  "clock": "Report cold start, full JSON elapsed from host request to parsed response, p95/p99/max, slow count, overage, cgroup limits, peak memory, total wall time, opponent search depth/change/zero and CPU activation per game. Report all host settings.",
